      "answer": "To pay off a $15,000 loan with 11% interest after 16 months, the amount of the single payment would be $17,780.80. To find the amount of the single payment that will pay off the $15,000 loan with 11% interest after 16 months, we can use the formula for calculating future value: Future Value = Principal + Interest Principal = $15,000 Interest rate = 11% per year (or 11/12% per month) Time = 16 months Using this information, we can calculate the future value: Future Value = $15,000 + ($15,000 * (11/12%) * 16) = $15,000 + ($15,000 * 0.00917 * 16) = $15,000 + $2,780.80 = $17,780.80 Therefore, the amount of the single payment at the end of 16 months would be $17,780.80.",
